WEBVTT

00:00:00.613 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.702 --> 00:00:04.270
Today we talk about extensions on forms.

00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:08.528
That means using builder gel to make the nail longer than the natural nail,

00:00:08.478 --> 00:00:10.510
on a form placed under the free edge.

00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:13.390
Well done extensions look really elegant.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.270
But done wrong, they break, lift, or tilt upwards like a ski jump.

00:00:18.681 --> 00:00:21.310
And a lot of these faults begin with the form itself.

00:00:21.864 --> 00:00:23.166
What is a form?

00:00:23.547 --> 00:00:25.086
There are two common kinds.

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:29.166
Paper forms, with adhesive, used once and thrown away.

00:00:29.524 --> 00:00:31.632
And metal forms, which can be reused,

00:00:31.582 --> 00:00:34.526
after cleaning and disinfecting like any other tool.

00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:37.086
The form is just a temporary mold.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:41.007
The gel sits on it and is cured, and then the form comes off,

00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:43.086
and the long nail stands on its own.

00:00:43.718 --> 00:00:49.250
Paper forms are soft, easy to cut to fit each nail, and always new for every client.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:52.978
Metal forms are rigid and keep a straight line very well,

00:00:52.928 --> 00:00:55.090
but you have to choose the right size,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.010
and process them after every client.

00:00:57.359 --> 00:00:58.690
Neither is clearly better.

00:00:59.061 --> 00:01:03.810
What matters is that the form fits snugly under the free edge of the client sitting in front of you.

00:01:04.458 --> 00:01:06.371
Not every nail should be extended.

00:01:06.784 --> 00:01:10.658
A natural nail bitten right down, with almost no free edge left,

00:01:10.608 --> 00:01:12.450
gives the form little support,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.011
and the extension has to carry almost everything.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.844
A nail with problems, such as separating from the bed, discoloration, or red,

00:01:20.794 --> 00:01:22.371
swollen skin around it,

00:01:22.629 --> 00:01:25.571
is not treated, and you advise the client to see a doctor.

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:29.171
You can review these signs in the lesson on when not to treat a client.

00:01:29.828 --> 00:01:33.582
The job of the form is to continue the line of the natural nail.

00:01:33.974 --> 00:01:38.115
Seen from the side, the form must run straight out from the free edge,

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:40.862
as if the natural nail had simply grown longer.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:45.569
Seen from above, and from the tip, the form lines up with the finger,

00:01:45.519 --> 00:01:47.822
not leaning left, not leaning right.

00:01:48.248 --> 00:01:51.582
However the form is placed, that is how the nail comes out.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.902
The gel just follows the form.

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:56.220
Here is something that happens a lot.

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:59.085
The technician places the form in a hurry,

00:01:59.035 --> 00:02:02.380
and there is a small gap between the free edge and the form.

00:02:02.808 --> 00:02:06.780
Gel runs down into that gap, and collects under the free edge.

00:02:07.151 --> 00:02:11.216
When the form comes off, there is a ridge of gel underneath the nail,

00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:12.380
the client feels it,

00:02:12.582 --> 00:02:13.580
and it traps dirt.

00:02:13.942 --> 00:02:18.066
And the extension is not joined to the natural nail, so it is weak,

00:02:18.016 --> 00:02:19.100
and lifts easily.

00:02:19.436 --> 00:02:22.780
That is why the form must fit tightly under the free edge.

00:02:23.021 --> 00:02:27.100
If needed, trim the curve of the form to fit the nail of each client.

00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:28.707
The next fault:

00:02:28.736 --> 00:02:29.827
a tilted form.

00:02:30.227 --> 00:02:33.907
If the form points down, the nail will curve down like a hook.

00:02:34.256 --> 00:02:37.747
If the form points up, the nail will tilt up like a ski jump.

00:02:38.174 --> 00:02:41.529
And if the form leans to one side, the nail will be crooked,

00:02:41.479 --> 00:02:43.347
with sides that are not parallel.

00:02:43.761 --> 00:02:46.646
These faults can hardly be rescued by filing afterwards,

00:02:46.596 --> 00:02:49.987
because the mistake is built into the whole structure of the nail.

00:02:50.151 --> 00:02:51.827
The way to avoid them is easy.

00:02:51.999 --> 00:02:55.587
Before you place the gel, look at the finger from three directions.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.387
It takes a few seconds, but it saves the whole set.

00:02:59.042 --> 00:03:00.248
Now about length.

00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:02.328
Think of an extension as a lever.

00:03:02.573 --> 00:03:03.906
The longer the extension,

00:03:03.856 --> 00:03:08.168
the more force goes to the stress area every time the tip knocks against something.

00:03:08.678 --> 00:03:11.848
The stress area is where the natural nail leaves the skin bed.

00:03:12.193 --> 00:03:14.888
So the length has to suit the natural nails of the client.

00:03:15.317 --> 00:03:18.728
If the natural nail is short and thin, do not make it too long.

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:22.408
And ask the client what they do for work, and in daily life.

00:03:22.837 --> 00:03:26.178
For someone who types all day, or works with their hands,

00:03:26.128 --> 00:03:28.488
a moderate length will last much longer.

00:03:28.825 --> 00:03:31.368
Be honest with the client, and they will trust you more.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.281
The structure is the same as in the builder gel theory lesson,

00:03:35.231 --> 00:03:36.420
so do review that one.

00:03:36.898 --> 00:03:38.180
Thin at the cuticle.

00:03:38.446 --> 00:03:39.540
Thin at the tip.

00:03:39.881 --> 00:03:42.980
Thickest at the apex, which sits over the stress area.

00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:46.740
Seen from the tip, the C curve is even on both sides.

00:03:47.008 --> 00:03:50.420
Seen from above, the side walls are straight and parallel.

00:03:50.838 --> 00:03:53.397
With extensions, the apex matters even more,

00:03:53.347 --> 00:03:56.420
because it has to carry the whole long part in front.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.517
The tip should be thin and refined, but not paper thin.

00:04:00.924 --> 00:04:04.197
People in the trade often compare it to the thickness of a bank card.

00:04:04.784 --> 00:04:07.797
Too thick, and the nail looks clumsy and heavy.

00:04:08.146 --> 00:04:10.677
Too thin, and the tip chips easily.

00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:15.056
And where the extension meets the natural nail, it must be seamless,

00:04:15.006 --> 00:04:16.517
with no step you can feel.

00:04:17.153 --> 00:04:19.651
There is one kind of break that is very common:

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:23.411
a straight break across the stress area, after just a few days.

00:04:23.732 --> 00:04:29.067
Seen from the side, the nail is flat and evenly thin, like a sheet of glass,

00:04:29.017 --> 00:04:29.971
with no apex.

00:04:30.389 --> 00:04:32.931
There was enough gel, but not in the right place:

00:04:33.202 --> 00:04:35.571
thin exactly where it needed to be thickest.

00:04:36.072 --> 00:04:40.451
The fix is not to build the whole nail thick, but to put the gel in the right place.

00:04:41.022 --> 00:04:41.987
The next fault:

00:04:42.092 --> 00:04:43.507
gel touching the skin.

00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:45.973
At the cuticle, in the side corners,

00:04:45.923 --> 00:04:49.106
or running over the edge of the form onto the fingertip.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:52.307
Uncured gel on the skin is the road to allergy.

00:04:52.655 --> 00:04:55.907
And where gel touches the skin, it lifts very quickly.

00:04:56.364 --> 00:04:58.627
Always leave a gap as thin as a hair.

00:04:58.971 --> 00:05:01.907
If some gets on the skin, wipe it off before curing.

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:04.718
For safety, remember two things.

00:05:05.063 --> 00:05:07.575
Switch on the dust extraction when filing,

00:05:07.525 --> 00:05:10.096
and cure for the full time the brand gives,

00:05:10.046 --> 00:05:14.318
because under cured gel is both weak and more likely to cause allergies.

00:05:14.803 --> 00:05:18.238
On allergies, review the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:05:18.322 --> 00:05:19.358
Just one sentence:

00:05:19.628 --> 00:05:23.678
uncured gel never touches the skin, neither the client nor yours.

00:05:24.305 --> 00:05:25.684
Then there are infills.

00:05:25.996 --> 00:05:29.853
As the nail grows out, the apex slowly moves towards the tip,

00:05:29.803 --> 00:05:32.724
the nail becomes top heavy, and breaks easily.

00:05:33.124 --> 00:05:36.964
Usually every three to four weeks, the client should come back for an infill.

00:05:37.304 --> 00:05:41.524
With infills on time, extensions last a long time and stay safe.

00:05:41.786 --> 00:05:44.143
Leave it too long, and the nail breaks easily,

00:05:44.093 --> 00:05:47.204
sometimes taking part of the natural nail underneath with it.

00:05:47.838 --> 00:05:48.400
You see.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.320
With extensions on forms, skilled hands are not enough.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.013
You have to place the form correctly, choose the right length,

00:05:55.963 --> 00:05:57.920
and put the apex in the right place.

00:05:58.348 --> 00:06:00.720
Once you understand it, your hands will follow.

00:06:01.134 --> 00:06:04.240
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step together.

00:06:04.431 --> 00:06:06.960
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:07.136 --> 00:06:08.000
See you next time.
